{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `7c9fd158`: the historical row stays in the held arm,\nand the arm carries the place of the entry.\n\n1. The row has another descriptor, so item 4 of `c79545a3` holds:\n   the client compares no meaning and shows no values. Neither of\n   the first two C3 rules applies, because each needs the present\n   meaning. Make no meaning for it.\n2. The entry is a fact that the replica verified, and the member\n   needs it. An act with this key took effect, and a member who\n   types the form again can make a second item. So the arm gains\n   one optional field: the place of the verified entry with this\n   key. It is evidence and no status. It does not say whether the\n   entry has the values that the member typed.\n3. The field is present for either reason of the arm when the\n   replica holds such an entry, and absent when it holds none.\n4. `restore(key)` still stops with `descriptor-mismatch`, so the\n   client makes no second act from this row. `dismiss(key)`\n   removes the row and leaves the record as it is.\n5. Add this combination to the historical case of\n   `scope-client.test.ts`: the key appears one time, in the arm,\n   with the place of the real entry.\n\nThe page words for this entry belong to the application. The\nimplementation note gives one example sentence.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}